  "problem": "If $z=-3-8\\text{i}$, then $z\\overset{\u2015}{z}=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=-3-8\\text{i},$ the real part is $\\text{Re}(z)=-3,$ and the imaginary part is $\\text{Im}(z)=-8,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{\u2015}{z} & =(\\text{Re}(z))^{2}+(\\text{Im}(z))^{2} \\\\  & =(-3)^{2}+(-8)^{2} \\\\  & =9+64 \\\\  & =73.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=-3-8\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{\u2015}{z}=-3+8\\text{i}.$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{\u2015}{z} & =(-3-8\\text{i})(-3+8\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(3)^{2}+(-3)(8)\\text{i}+(-8)(-3)\\text{i}-{\\text{i}}^{2}(8)^{2} \\\\  & =9-\\cancel{24\\text{i}}+\\cancel{24\\text{i}}-(-1)(64) \\\\  & =9+64 \\\\  & =73.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
